emails.body_template:
Team,

After yesterday's meeting, here's our finalized timeline:

- Manager training: Next {meeting_day}
- Review cycle launch: {deadline}
- 360 feedback collection: Week 2-3
- Final reviews due: End of month

Please confirm this works with your schedules and departmental commitments. Once approved, {hr_generalist_name} will send the announcement to all managers.

{hr_director_name}

{recruiter_name},

The nursing shortage is indeed critical. I've reviewed your strategy and it's comprehensive.

{hr_director_name} - We need executive approval for the sign-on bonus budget. Can you present this to leadership?

{hr_generalist_name} - Please coordinate with Finance on budget allocation for the campaign.

Target launch date: {deadline}

{hr_manager_name}

Hi team,

I've contacted the vendor (ThermoFisher) and scheduled:

- Instrument installation: Next {meeting_day}
- Technical training: {meeting_day} and {meeting_day}
- Applications training: Following week

They'll provide 100 control samples for initial validation. The system requires dedicated workspace - I've identified the alcove next to our PCR setup.

Do we need any special ventilation or biosafety considerations beyond our current BSL-2 setup?

Also, should I coordinate with IT for LIS integration?

{lab_technician_name}

I can take Saturday MRI 8 AM - 4 PM, but I have a conflict Sunday morning. Could someone else handle MRI on-call Sunday?

Also, do we have the portable MRI scheduled for any emergency department cases this weekend?

{mri_tech_name}

Good work, team. I'm approving emergency contractor rates if we can get someone here sooner. {facilities_manager_name}, please coordinate with nursing leadership to ensure patient safety protocols are in place.

I'll notify the CMO about the situation. Let's aim for full resolution by end of day.

{facilities_director_name}

Reviewed the safety protocols - they look good. Just one addition: we need to ensure all electrical isolation procedures are followed for the MRI-compatible equipment.

Also, the new FDA guidelines require additional documentation for Class III devices. I'll send you the updated forms.

{safety_officer_name}

Absolutely, {facilities_manager_name}. My team is available for equipment transport. We'll need advance notice for the heavier units.

I suggest we start with the OR equipment during the scheduled maintenance window next {meeting_day}.

{maintenance_supervisor_name}
